根据古诗词创作一张新中式细线设色装饰插画海报，将诗中的景物、空间与情感转化为完整的东方诗意场景。

采用高位俯瞰、东方散点透视与现代平面构成。树冠呈柔软蓬松的云团状色块，具有细腻粉末点染质感，内部穿插纤细连续的墨黑枝条。传统建筑使用精细工笔线描、规整青绿瓦片、白墙朱柱。地面与水面采用大面积暖米白留白，搭配少量不规则墨黑阴影。

配色采用饱满、干净、哑光的东方传统色系，以主色形成视觉重量，辅以石青、石绿、朱砂、赭红等颜色，保持细腻统一的纸本装饰插画质感。

画面突出核心意象，通过自然曲线、色块包围和疏密对比建立视觉层次。构图随诗词内容变化，不强行加入无关建筑或树木。

融入大幅暖白色中文标题、小型纵排诗句、作者署名与少量朱印，形成完整的古诗词艺术海报。

避免写实山水、厚重水墨、3D、油画、动漫风、复杂远景、过度颗粒及人工做旧。保持教科书级的精细线条、柔和设色与东方装饰美学。

Prompt:

Theme: {cultural event, craft workshop, exhibition, or creative gathering}
Main palette: {2 to 4 colors}
Structural method: {layered cutouts, dark framing, color overprint, folded planes, or another paper construction}
Micro scene: {a tiny workshop, performance, or making process}
Title: {event title}
Event details: {optional date, venue, activity}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a refined vertical cultural poster using tactile handmade paper, large color fields, structural composition, and a tiny narrative scene.

Build the main visual with a clear paper based construction method. The composition may use layered apertures, framing, overlapping printed blocks, folded planes, or other physical paper relationships. Let the structure itself create depth, rhythm, and visual tension rather than relying on decorative graphics.

All large paper areas should have realistic handmade texture, including visible fibers, pulp variation, pigment absorption, subtle pressure marks, irregular edges, and slight material imperfections. Keep the surfaces matte, clean, and sophisticated.

Use strong but controlled color relationships. Large color fields should remain visually clear from a distance, while smaller overlaps, cut edges, shadows, folds, and paper thickness become visible only when viewed closely.

Add one small micro scene related to the theme. Include two or three adult figures naturally performing the activity, such as cutting paper, operating a press, performing shadow theatre, folding structures, or arranging materials. Keep the entire scene around 3% to 5% of the poster so it remains a discovered detail rather than the main subject.

Use generous warm ivory or neutral negative space to balance the large structural forms.

Typography should be restrained and secondary. Use a refined editorial serif for the main title and small uppercase sans serif for supporting information. Keep the title relatively small and place it in a quiet area of the composition.

The visual reading order should be:

large paper structure first, color and material interaction second, micro scene third, title and event information last.

The final result should feel contemporary, tactile, editorial, architectural, and handmade. From a distance, the poster should read as a strong abstract composition. Up close, it should reveal paper fibers, cut edges, folds, overlaps, print texture, tiny people, tools, and process.

Prompt:

【Series Name】: {e.g. FOCAL IDENTITY}  
【Main Title】: {e.g. MOTION / OBSERVE / SIGNAL / FRAME}  
【Subject】: {age, gender, identity, profession}  
【Name】: {name}  
【Role】: {profession / creative role}  
【Key Line】: {short concept-driven sentence}  
【Accent Color】: {yellow / red / cobalt blue / rust orange}  
【Focus Method】: {horizontal sharp slice / floating focus window / vertical sharp slice / offset focus frame}  
【Aspect Ratio】: 9:16

Create a sophisticated editorial portrait poster built around selective focus. Use a realistic photographic portrait with natural skin texture, pores, subtle imperfections, believable hair, and authentic facial structure. Avoid plastic skin, CGI smoothness, heavy beauty retouching, or generic commercial-model styling.

Keep most of the portrait softly blurred, slightly motion-softened, desaturated, or reduced in detail. Only the selected 【Focus Method】 should return to sharp detail, natural skin tone, and clear texture. The sharp and blurred areas must remain perfectly aligned as the same person and the same photographic moment, with no duplicated eyes, second face, or pasted-photo effect.

Choose one focus structure: a horizontal sharp band across the eyes, a small floating window isolating part of the face, a narrow vertical sharp slice through motion blur, or a larger offset frame that deliberately shifts attention away from the facial center.

Use a restrained neutral palette of charcoal, gray, warm beige, off-white, and natural skin tones. Use 【Accent Color】 as the only strong accent for the focus lines, main title, and a few key details. Keep the visual rule: Neutral Field + One Accent Color.

Use mature magazine-style typography: a high-contrast editorial serif for 【Main Title】, a condensed bold sans serif for 【Name】 and 【Role】, and a small neutral sans serif for secondary information. Include 【Key Line】 as meaningful copy connected to the subject and concept, not random filler text.

Keep the composition asymmetric with generous negative space. Let the portrait, typography, and focus geometry interact naturally. Add subtle film grain, light scan texture, and restrained print texture so the whole poster feels like one finished editorial piece.

The final result should feel like a polished independent fashion, photography, music, or culture magazine poster, with blur and sharpness deliberately controlling where the viewer looks.

Avoid cyberpunk HUDs, excessive UI graphics, neon gradients, gibberish text, logos, watermarks, numbering, sparkle symbols, harsh Gaussian blur, melted facial features, duplicated features, plastic skin, and over-retouching.

